RISE ASCII SCENE 7
#############################################################################################################
#   VCM torture test: "SDF luminaire jellyfish"                                                             #
#   An underwater tableau -- a sea turtle banking over a coral reef, a jellyfish drifting at right, all      #
#   inside a scattering water volume under a displaced dielectric surface.  Built by a GUI agent session;    #
#   banked here for the transport stress it puts on VCM, not for its picture.                                #
#############################################################################################################

#############################################################################################################
#   SESSION PROVENANCE                                                                                      #
#                                                                                                           #
#   Prompt (verbatim, the user's own words):                                                                #
#     "Build an underwater world filled with interesting sea creatures, corals and other interesting        #
#      objects.  Make the lighting dramatic but realistic.  The scene should also be colorful but also      #
#      realistic and creatively use materials and shapes."                                                  #
#   (The trajectory's user record also carries a bracketed restatement from the intake assistant, marked    #
#   informational-only in the record itself.  It is not reproduced here as authored intent.)                #
#                                                                                                           #
#   Model:    provider `gemini`.  All 51 agent turns in the trajectory record                               #
#             gen_ai.request.model = gemini-3.5-flash.  The single populate_scene completion reports        #
#             model gemini-3.6-flash in its own result.  Both values are as recorded; the brief that        #
#             commissioned this reconstruction said gemini-3.6-flash, which matches only that one call.     #
#   Date:     2026-08-13 (session started 14:14:51Z).  RISE GUI agent session.                              #
#   Session:  trace c04ad682-ce1b-41ce-a80d-8d76f338c355                                                    #
#   Trajectory: ~/Library/Application Support/RISE/trajectories/gui/20260813T141451Z-c04ad682.jsonl         #
#############################################################################################################

#############################################################################################################
#   RECONSTRUCTION NOTE -- THIS FILE IS A RECONSTRUCTION, NOT THE SCENE THE SESSION SAVED.                  #
#                                                                                                           #
#   The owner closed the app without saving.  This file was rebuilt from the session trajectory: the LAST   #
#   read_document result (full document text at head revision 58, which already contains all four           #
#   build_element outputs) plus every recorded mutating call after it, applied in recorded order and ONLY   #
#   where the recorded result says it applied.  place_element transforms were re-applied by a port of the   #
#   engine's own composition -- AgentSession::PlaceElement, plus RotateEulerDeg_ / FormatVec3_ -- not by    #
#   approximation; all six calls reproduce their recorded patch counts exactly (6, 6, 21, 9, 14, 21).       #
#                                                                                                           #
#   KNOWN GAPS -- what is NOT here, and why:                                                                #
#                                                                                                           #
#   1. THE FIVE populate_scene REPEATS ARE ABSENT.  populate_scene created corals_stem1_extra1,             #
#      corals_stem2_extra1, corals_polyps_extra1, corals_stem1_extra2 and corals_polyps_extra2 (reusing     #
#      the corals geometries and materials).  The trajectory records their names, geometry and material     #
#      but NOT their positions, so they cannot be replaced without inventing coordinates.  They are         #
#      omitted rather than guessed.  Measured effect: this scene has 18 objects where the session's final   #
#      render had 23.                                                                                      #
#                                                                                                           #
#   2. THREE RECORDED CALLS ARE DELIBERATELY NOT APPLIED, because they did not apply in the session         #
#      either: two insert_chunks batches refused (zero-area-light gate, then compose-phase geometry gate)   #
#      and one remove_chunks refused (compose-phase form-bearing gate).  The identical third insert and     #
#      the post-reopen remove DID apply and ARE here.                                                       #
#                                                                                                           #
#   3. TWO RASTERIZER CHUNKS ARE PRESENT, as in the session: the starter's pathtracing_pel_rasterizer and   #
#      the inserted vcm_pel_rasterizer.  Unnamed chunks derive last-wins, so VCM is the active integrator   #
#      -- which is exactly what every recorded render result reports.  Left as authored; do not "tidy".     #
#                                                                                                           #
#   FIDELITY vs THE SESSION'S LAST RECORDED RENDER (256x192, 16 spp, VCM):                                  #
#     every object's world bbox centre matches to the printed precision (17 of 17 shared objects);          #
#     FRAME TONE luma mean 39.2 here vs 39.0 recorded, stddev 13.44 vs 13.60, mode 40 vs 40,                #
#     P1/P99 12/97 vs 13/97; meanRGB (0.00713, 0.03684, 0.08764) vs (0.00691, 0.03671, 0.08767).            #
#     The residual is the five absent coral repeats: they occluded ~112 px of water_volume and ~7 px of     #
#     corals_stem2_obj in the recorded frame.                                                               #
#############################################################################################################

#############################################################################################################
#   WHY IT IS HELD -- WHAT THIS SCENE STRESSES                                                              #
#                                                                                                           #
#   Emissive materials on SDF geometry, inside a dielectric bell, inside a scattering medium.  The three    #
#   jellyfish materials are pbr_metallic_roughness_material with an `emissive` painter and an               #
#   emissive_scale (jellyfish_bell_emit at 0.4, jellyfish_core_emit at 0.8, jellyfish_tentacle_emit at      #
#   0.7) -- NOT lambertian_luminaire_material; there is no lambertian_luminaire chunk anywhere in this      #
#   scene or in the session that built it.  Each is bound to an sdf_geometry at sampling_detail 64.         #
#                                                                                                           #
#   That combination exercises the CanBeAreaLight guard in BOTH directions in one load:                     #
#     * jellyfish_bell_geo and jellyfish_core_geo area-sample cleanly, so NEE gets to area-sample an        #
#       IMPLICIT surface and VCM gets to emit light subpaths and photons from one -- through the            #
#       surrounding dielectric bell, which is S-D-S transport;                                             #
#     * jellyfish_tentacles_geo does NOT.  Its capsule radii (0.006 to 0.018) fall below the sampling       #
#       grid, so SDFGeometry reports "sampling mesh PROVABLY missed surface in 77 grid cell(s)",            #
#       CanBeAreaLight() returns false, and LuminaryManager drops it from light sampling -- it still        #
#       contributes emission on direct camera view and BSDF-sampled hits.  Both warnings fire on every      #
#       load of this file.  They are the point, not a defect to fix: raising sampling_detail would          #
#       silence the case this scene exists to hold.                                                        #
#                                                                                                           #
#   Layered on top: a homogeneous_medium interior (absorption 0.04 0.005 0.001, scattering 0.02 0.02 0.03,  #
#   HG g=0.4) filling a box that contains everything; a displaced_geometry dielectric water surface at      #
#   ior 1.333 above it; a directional sun at power 120 through that surface; and a radiance_background      #
#   environment.  So the SDF sampling cache, the area-light guard, volumetric transport and a refractive    #
#   boundary are all under load in the same frame.                                                          #
#                                                                                                           #
#   HONEST CAVEATS, measured not assumed:                                                                   #
#     * The corals are misplaced.  corals_stem1_obj and corals_stem2_obj have world bbox centres at         #
#       z = +26 and z = +31 -- far behind the camera plane -- because their SDF capsule parts carry         #
#       rotations that place_element's scale-then-offset composition carried outward.  This is faithful     #
#       to the session: the recorded final render reports the same centres. It is not a reconstruction      #
#       error.                                                                                              #
#     * The `pixel_filter box` and 16-sample settings are the agent's, kept as authored.                    #
#     * validate reports one info diagnostic (DESIGN_SCALAR_PIPE_UNUSED); the session's own validate call   #
#       reported the same one.                                                                              #
#############################################################################################################

#############################################################################################################
#   MEASURED PT-vs-VCM A/B -- RESOLVED 2026-08-13 (same day it was banked).                                 #
#                                                                                                           #
#   The original A/B (kept in git history at 07f04ba2) read: PT stable at luma-mean 18.2 (PNG 0-255),       #
#   VCM at ~40 with non-shrinking speckle and an upward drift, and honestly declined to say which was       #
#   right.  The investigation (docs/SUBMERGED_CAMERA_IOR_SEEDING.md) proved THE 2.2x "VCM EXCESS WAS        #
#   PT'S DEFICIT: PathTracingIntegrator never seeded its eye-ray IOR stack from the camera position         #
#   (IORStackSeeding::SeedFromPoint -- BDPT/VCM always did), and this camera sits INSIDE water_volume's     #
#   closed dielectric boundary, so PT misclassified every outward crossing as an entry and                  #
#   DielectricSPF dropped the transmission lobe -- losing ~4.4x of the scene's environment transport.       #
#   A closed-form micro-scene (camera in a delta-dielectric shell, uniform env; every pixel must equal      #
#   the env colour exactly) arbitrated: PT rendered 0.0, VCM/BDPT rendered it exactly.  Now a permanent     #
#   regression: EnvLightBalanceTest topology J "submerged camera".                                          #
#                                                                                                           #
#   POST-FIX A/B (400x300, raw EXR, linear Rec.709 luma -- NOT comparable to the old PNG 0-255 numbers):    #
#                                                                                                           #
#     integrator          spp    wall     luma mean    mean|neighbour diff|                                 #
#     pathtracing_pel     256    21.8 s    0.05330          0.0067                                          #
#     pathtracing_pel    1024    87.1 s    0.05328          0.0048                                          #
#     vcm_pel             256    15.7 s    0.04151          0.0223                                          #
#     vcm_pel            1024    60.4 s    0.04147          0.0162                                          #
#                                                                                                           #
#   Both integrators are now FLAT across a 4x sample increase; the "VCM mean drift" did not survive the     #
#   linear-EXR re-measurement.  VCM's residual 0.78x vs PT is measured, attributed, and documented in       #
#   docs/SUBMERGED_CAMERA_IOR_SEEDING.md: (a) VCM/BDPT take no NEE and no merges at MEDIUM vertices, so     #
#   env/omni in-scatter through the water medium is under-counted (env-only split: VCM/PT = 0.854, BDPT     #
#   identical); (b) VCM never samples the directional sun AT ALL (radiantExitance()==0 keeps it out of      #
#   the alias table and VCM lacks PT/BDPT's deterministic zero-exitance NEE loop; no-env split: 0.649).     #
#   VCM's higher neighbour-diff DOES converge (splat variance through the diffuse-transmissive box          #
#   boundary, not bias).  Two more traps this scene documents: dielectric `scattering 0.0` means            #
#   MAXIMALLY DIFFUSE transmission, not "off" (the water box is a diffuse transmitter, kept as              #
#   authored); and the jellyfish emitters' `scale 1.3` exposed Object::GetArea() ignoring the               #
#   transform's area Jacobian (fixed the same day; GeometryUVRoundtripTest::TestObjectWorldArea).           #
#                                                                                                           #
#   The scene remains held for: submerged-camera IOR seeding, the CanBeAreaLight both-directions load,      #
#   the VCM directional-light + medium-vertex gaps quantified above, and as the origin scene of             #
#   docs/skills/bdpt-vcm-mis-balance.md's step-0 cause #0.                                                  #
#############################################################################################################


